<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. van Beethoven is a 30-year-old pianist and composer with asymmetric bilateral sensorineural hearing loss, bilateral tinnitus, and an adjustment disorder with depressed mood, who comes for his yearly preventive visit six weeks after his three-month review. He wears both hearing aids most of the day and uses the music program at the piano. The tinnitus is still there but quieter in his mind, and he sleeps through most nights with a sound machine. He has had four more sessions of cognitive behavioral therapy. He went to two small dinners with friends this month, his first gatherings in two years, and followed most of the talk at a table for four. His mood is steady, and his PHQ-9 today is 5. He has no new concerns. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 30</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Hearing aids worn most of the day; no change in hearing noticed</td></tr><tr><td>Tinnitus</td><td>Constant but less intrusive; sleeping with sound enrichment</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 5; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient in writing before the visit and reviewed with him face to face by Dr. Vandermeer; he wore his hearing aids, and the remote microphone was used in the room. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Seeing friends again in small groups; work is going well; still keeps his hearing private from most colleagues</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and communication</td><td>Hearing aids daily; remote microphone for teaching; live speech-to-text on his phone in meetings</td></tr><tr><td>Substance use</td><td>Wine with dinner three or four evenings a week, two glasses at most; no tobacco or drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Walks for an hour most afternoons</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Irregular meals on long working days</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours on most nights with a sound machine</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>Not currently in a relationship; no new partners this year</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe; a flashing smoke alarm and doorbell installed</td></tr><tr><td>Road safety</td><td>Does not drive; wears a seat belt</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Noise</td><td>Wears musicians&apos; earplugs in loud rehearsals</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

