    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. Tetanus booster due and given; HIV screening not yet done. [S]<list><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Asymmetric bilateral sensorineural hearing loss with hearing aids (H90.3)</content>. Using his aids most of the day with good benefit. Some soft wax in the left canal, not blocking it; hearing aid users build up wax faster. [S]<list><item>Repeat audiogram at the six-month visit.</item><item>Clean the aid domes daily; do not use cotton swabs; come in if the left ear feels blocked.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Adjustment disorder with depressed mood (F43.21)</content>. Improving with therapy and a return to small gatherings; PHQ-9 5. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline is saved in his phone with its text option. [S]<list><item>Continue cognitive behavioral therapy every two weeks.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Long-standing loose stools and abdominal discomfort</content>. Unchanged for years, with no blood, weight loss, night symptoms, or anemia (hemoglobin normal at intake). No alarm features. [S]<list><item>Offered further evaluation; he prefers to keep a symptom diary and discuss it again at the next visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>118/76 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 5, from 12 at intake; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>AUDIT-C 3 at intake, below the threshold for men; drinking unchanged by his report</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening for adults 15 to 65; antigen-antibody test drawn today with his agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Antibody nonreactive at intake (signal-to-cutoff 0.08)</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Triple panel at intake: surface antigen and core antibody nonreactive; surface antibody 64 mIU/mL, immune from childhood vaccination</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>HbA1c 5.2% at intake; not overweight enough to meet the screening criterion before 35; statin assessment begins at 40</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Under audiology and otolaryngology care; repeat audiogram at six months</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Tdap given today; last dose more than ten years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza and COVID-19 vaccines, this season</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza vaccine at the six-month visit in October; COVID-19 vaccine discussed and he will decide then</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Shared decision-making for adults 27 to 45; he chose not to have it</td></tr><tr><td>Skin cancer counseling and dental care</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Sun protection discussed; dental visit within the year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap vaccine [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Six-month review in eight weeks with a repeat audiogram and the influenza vaccine. HIV result through the patient portal, as he asked. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: six-month review with repeat audiogram. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

