    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 17 minutes, with his consent, held face to face with his hearing aids and the remote microphone, and summarized for him in writing. He named a close friend as his health care agent, and a health care proxy form was completed; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He said that what matters most to him is being able to keep composing, that he wants to be told the truth about his health in writing as well as aloud, and that he wants clinicians to face him and speak plainly rather than shout. He chose not to record specific treatment preferences today. The plan will be revisited yearly or after any serious illness. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
